worst fiber (256,121): a= 50895  b= 61952
  C=max(a^2,b^2)= 3838050304   log C= 22.068230341272496
  R=rad(a b |a^2-b^2|)= 452572850730   log R= 26.83821458321631
  log C / log R = 0.8222689431462108  (ABC-quality; ABC conj => ->1)
  6*logC/logR = 4.933613658877265  (upper proxy for sigma; true sigma=4.614)

UNCONDITIONAL Stewart-Yu form (abc II, Math Ann 291 (1991), refined Stewart-Yu 2001):
  log C <= kappa * R^{1/3} * (log R)^3   (kappa effective, ~ explicit)
  => sigma <= 6 log C / log R <= 6 kappa R^{1/3} (log R)^2.
  This is the BEST provable UNCONDITIONAL bound: sigma = O(N^{1/3}(log N)^2).
  It GROWS with N -- NOT a constant. Only ABC/Szpiro gives the constant 6+eps.
